{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id180370440"}, "name":{"label":"Roaring_T_Rex"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2025-08-03T17:37:10-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.6.15.0"}, "id":{"label":"12972911344"}, "title":{"label":"Cutscene bug."}, "content":{"label":"Some of the cutscenes are completely buggy.  You can see the start of them, but it’s only you and the townsperson waiting around, and nothing happens at all.  You can’t move.  You can’t click on anything but “skip”.\n\nI’ve played this game on p.c.  And comparing this to that, i think the problem is cutscenes in which the player must move around.  It’s at Robin’s house, the beach for Haley, at the decorative tree in C. forest for Leah, and probably more. Perhaps it’s the combination of this and my controls.  But i can’t quickly switch controls before these cutscenes, because i don’t know when they’ll happen.  I use the controls of “invisible joystick & 2 buttons”.\n\nAlso, the sling shot carnival game doesn’t work at all, because the player is at the bottom of the screen.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=1406710800&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"1"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"1"}}, 
